Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:23:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11152/11171] [outer-loop] Record the round-two agent as
 in-flight state

A second subagent is running in an isolated worktree. Written down so an
unexplained branch or worktree found later has an owner, and so round one's
already-merged branch is not confused with it.

Also records in memory that a green sharded test run is not evidence the suite
collects: three test files were un-collectable for five days while every
per-task conductor phase passed, because a shard that excludes a broken file
cannot report it. The cheap check is --collect-only over the whole tree.

That memory entry also carries the counting error I made while sizing the
problem, since the method matters more than the number: counting test files
whose carnot module is absent gave 1776 of 3902 and measured a path convention
rather than breakage. The honest figure was the 3 pytest had already printed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
